{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The governing measurement is the trace, and on this trip it clears the establishment gate but stops well short of materiality. EV-GPS-00501 is complete and unimpaired — 163 fixes at a 10 s cadence, 100% coverage, zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s, so none of the POL-RD-07(a)-(c) impairment conditions is met — and it records trace_distance_km 25.4 against an optimal of 19.6 km, an excess of 5.8 km and 29.6%. POL-RD-01 makes that deviation ESTABLISHED (over 20% and over 0.8 km) but not MATERIAL, because it is under both the 50% and the 8.0 km lines; the escalated consequences POL-RD-06 attaches to materiality therefore never arise. The driver does not dispute the establishment finding; he disputes what follows from it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00501", "EV-TRIP-00501"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern exists against this driver, and none may be built from his record. POL-RD-06's consultation was not even triggered, because the deviation is not material; and if it is run anyway it returns nothing: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over completed_trips_90d of 250, so neither the '3 or more flags' limb nor the '0.05 ratio with at least 40 trips' limb is satisfied. There is accordingly no balance-tilt toward the rider, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is not the trailing-90-day field POL-RD-06 names and may not be substituted for it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00501"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare model closes the refund the rider is really asking for. fare_breakdown.fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE and quoted_fare_sgd is 24.50, so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run: the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, a detour costs the rider nothing on those lines, and no distance-or-time refund is available however large the 5.8 km excess is. The SGD 14.50 the claim rests on is nothing more than charged_total 39.00 less quoted_fare_sgd 24.50 — a gap between two totals, not a loss the rider bore on distance or time. On this fare model the extra kilometres are the driver's loss, and he has already absorbed them.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00501", "EV-TRIP-00501"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_over_quote",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither ERP line is a phantom charge, so no billing-integrity refund is due under POL-RD-09(4). The trace carries a fix 0.0 m from the ECP (Fort Rd towards City) gantry — fix index 101 at 14:28:30, the exact timestamp at which the first SGD 3.00 was charged — and a fix 0.0 m from the ECP (Rochor towards City) gantry — fix index 130 at 14:33:20, the exact timestamp of the second SGD 3.00. Both are far inside POL-RD-09's 250 m match radius, so both gantries were actually crossed by this vehicle on this trip. There is nothing unmatched here for the rider to have refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00501", "EV-FARE-00501"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Run POL-RD-11(a) as written and the refund is small. The rider's remedy is the amount by which charged_total exceeds quoted_fare_sgd plus the pass-through lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09, and POL-RD-11(a) describes that basket as 'ERP and tolls actually crossed' — not as gantries on the optimal route. POL-RD-09(1)'s on-optimal-route-only treatment is expressly tied to a POL-RD-02 refund, and POL-RD-11 says POL-RD-02 does not run on an upfront-quoted trip. Deducting only the two ERP lines actually crossed (SGD 6.00), the refund is 39.00 - (24.50 + 6.00) = SGD 8.50. It is not the SGD 14.50 the claim implies, and it is not the full SGD 39.00 contested.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00501", "EV-GPS-00501"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.off_optimal_route_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The basket is in fact wider still, and the refund correspondingly smaller. This trip ORIGINATES at Changi Terminal 3, so under the fare model an off-peak Changi surcharge of SGD 6.00 is properly chargeable on it, and the ledger applied 0.00 of it. POL-RD-11(a) names 'a properly chargeable airport surcharge' in the deduction — properly chargeable, not merely charged — so the basket is 24.50 + 6.00 (ERP actually crossed) + 6.00 (properly chargeable surcharge) = 36.50, and the refund is 39.00 - 36.50 = SGD 2.50. On either reading of the basket the rider's complaint of being overcharged is answered: the charged total does not even reach what the rate card entitled the driver to bill.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00501", "EV-FARE-00501"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not ask to be exonerated on the strength of any rider instruction, and the record would not let him. The chat log for this trip carries zero messages (message_count 0, truncated false), so no rider instruction is recorded, no waypoint_hint exists and the corroboration POL-RD-04 requires — the vehicle passing within 200 m of a requested waypoint, or travelling a named road — cannot be run. POL-RD-04 itself directs that the clause is then unavailable and the case is decided on the remaining clauses, which is precisely what the driver asks for. Nothing in the record contradicts the driver's contemporaneous account; the money is fixed by POL-RD-11 either way.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00501", "EV-TRIP-00501"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver likewise claims no closure or traffic-event exoneration, and none is available: the only TRAFFIC_ADVISORY artifact in the pool, EV-ADVIS-00501-01, is MISSING — no payload, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT — so no advisory names any road or segment this route traverses. Under POL-RD-08 a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, discharges nothing, and the driver does not rest on it. He rests instead on POL-RD-11, which operates on the face of the ledger (fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 24.50) and limits the rider's remedy without any finding about the driver's conduct. The detour is conceded at 5.8 km and 29.6%; its consequence is the non-material one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00501-01", "EV-FARE-00501"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 8.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this is an upfront-quoted trip, and that decides most of the case. EV-FARE-00501 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 24.50 against total_charged 39.00, so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run. The deviation itself is established on the governing measurement: POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the field, and EV-GPS-00501 gives 25.4 km against an optimal of 19.6 km - an excess of 5.8 km / 29.6%, which clears the 20% and 0.8 km gates but stays under the 50% and 8.0 km materiality lines. So no POL-RD-06 uplift and no conduct referral arise (and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over completed_trips_90d 250 in any event; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only). Under upfront pricing the extra distance and time are the driver's to absorb and are not refundable to the rider as such. What the rider is entitled to under POL-RD-11(a) is the amount by which charged_total exceeds quoted_fare_sgd plus the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable. The raw over-quote is 39.00 - 24.50 = 14.50, and that figure must be adjusted for the pass-through lines. (1) The two ECP ERP charges (3.00 + 3.00 = 6.00 on EV-FARE-00501) were genuinely incurred - each matches a trace fix at 0.0 m - so there is no phantom line and no billing-integrity refund under POL-RD-09(4). But both gantries lie off the optimal corridor (on_optimal_route false; the optimal PIE-Nicoll corridor carries no ERP), and no rider instruction caused the detour, so under POL-RD-09 and POL-RD-11(b) they are corrected once: the rider does not ultimately bear them, and they are not stacked on top of any other figure. (2) The trip ORIGINATES at Changi Terminal 3 (EV-TRIP-00501) and was taken off-peak, so under the fare model an airport surcharge of SGD 6.00 is properly chargeable. The ledger itemised 0.00, but POL-RD-11(a) counts a properly chargeable surcharge, not merely a charged one, so the rider properly owes the quote plus that 6.00. Refund = 39.00 - (24.50 + 6.00) = SGD 8.50. On the arguments: the rider's claim to the full 14.50 is rejected because it leaves the properly chargeable SGD 6.00 airport surcharge out of the reckoning; her point that the SGD 6.00 ERP must not be double-counted is right and is given effect (corrected once, not stacked). The driver's alternative that the refund is only 2.50 is rejected because it would make the rider bear the off-route ECP ERP, which POL-RD-11(b) and POL-RD-09 correct; the 8.50 he also offers is the correct figure. His 'she agreed to take ECP' account has no artifact behind it: EV-CHAT-00501 contains zero messages, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run, the clause is unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 a bare assertion in a statement does not discharge his burden. His PIE-congestion point is a general traffic assertion with no advisory behind it; the only advisory in the pool (EV-ADVIS-00501-01) is MISSING at weight 0.0 and he does not rest on POL-RD-03, so it changes nothing. No escalation is triggered: the trace is complete and unimpaired on POL-RD-07 (163 fixes, 10 s cadence, no gaps, 0.0 s maximum gap), the trip identifiers match, and the timestamps are consistent. No referral is ordered - no repeat-deviation pattern (POL-RD-06(c)), no phantom gantry (POL-RD-09(4)) and no no-show or false-arrival issue. Confidence 0.85; every deciding fact rests on artifacts at weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
